# The official image is built from a repository checkout, not from this folder.
# Keeping the build context out of the image matters: `bin/`, `obj/` and the committed sample
# databases would otherwise be copied in and, worse, invalidate the restore layer on every build.
bin/
obj/
**/bin/
**/obj/

.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
artifacts/

# docs/ is documentation, not build input — with one exception. The dashboard project copies
# observability/grafana-dashboard.json into its build output, so that folder has to reach the
# context or publish fails with MSB3030. Excluding docs/* rather than docs/ keeps the parent
# traversable, which is what makes the negation below reliable.
docs/*
!docs/observability

# A committed store must never become the image's initial database.
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm

**/*.user
